    "urlId" : "2024/july-19-post-power-shared-meal",
    "title" : "The Power of a Shared Meal",
    "sourceUrl" : "",
    "body" : "<div class=\"sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12\" data-layout-label=\"Post Body\" data-type=\"item\" id=\"item-669a99e304b03b42eeb55495\"><div class=\"row sqs-row\"><div class=\"col sqs-col-12 span-12\"><div class=\"sqs-block website-component-block sqs-block-website-component sqs-block-html html-block\" data-block-css=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/cc58a320-ef63-4275-ac16-b0b276e029f1_983/website.components.html.styles.css&quot;]\" data-block-scripts=\"[&quot;https://definitions.sqspcdn.com/website-component-definition/static-assets/website.components.html/cc58a320-ef63-4275-ac16-b0b276e029f1_983/website.components.html.visitor.js&quot;]\" data-block-type=\"1337\" data-definition-name=\"website.components.html\" data-sqsp-block=\"text\" data-website-component-id=\"0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e\" id=\"block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e\"><div class=\"sqs-block-content\"><div class=\"sqs-text-block-container\">\n  \n  <div class=\"sqs-html-content\" data-sqsp-text-block-content><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\">There\u2019s something incredible that happens when people sit down together and break bread. Not just for friends and family, but even for people who have deep divisions and don\u2019t like each other. There\u2019s a growing body of literature on this topic which goes by names like </span><a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2023/12/25/opinion/culinary-diplomacy-state-dinners.html\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\">\u201Cculinary diplomacy.\u201D</span></span></a><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\"> We have noted the power and potential, and for this reason we include a shared meal as part of our Heart &amp; Mind Conversations. This process was incorporated a few years into in an intriguing television program called \"Breaking Borders\" from the Travel Channel. This unique show combined great cooking with meal conversations between enemies. Unfortunately, it was limited to one season. Click this </span><a href=\"https://vimeo.com/257502083\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\">link</span></span></a><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\"> to watch the episode that is still timely titled <em>Israel/Palestine</em> at the Vimeo page of the show\u2019s producer Brian Leonard. </span></p><p class=\"\" data-rte-preserve-empty=\"true\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"></p><p class=\"\" style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;\"><span class=\"sqsrte-text-color--black\">WHAT IF a new series of short videos, or a series was produced, that tapped into the science of conflict and brought people together over a common meal and strategic conversations geared toward creating openness and trust-building?</span></p></div>\n\n\n  \n<style id=\"container-styles\">#block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e {\n    \n    --stroke-style: none;--stroke-thickness: 6px;\n    \n      \n      \n      \n    \n\n\n\n  }\n\n  #block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e .sqs-html-content {\n    \n    --tweak-text-block-padding: 6% 6% 6% 6%;\n  --tweak-text-block-padding: initial;\n}\n\n  #block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e {\n      mix-blend-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend\n  );\n      border-radius: var(--tweak-text-block-radius);\n  }\n\n  \n  \n#block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e {\n      --tweak-text-block-radius: 0px 0px 0px 0px;\n    }\n\n\n  \n  \n\n  #block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e {\n    }\n\n</style>\n\n<style id=\"override-container-styles\">\n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n            \n\n#block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  \n    @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          #block-0e279c2ca212c87b4e1e .sqs-html-content {\n            \n            }\n        }\n    \n  @media screen and (max-width: 767px) {\n          \n          \n\n          \n          \n          \n        }</style>\n<style class=\"transform-overrides-vars\">\n  \n</style>\n\n\n\n\n</div>\n</div></div></div></div></div>",
